person.about_me:
- 5 years at Accenture as a business strategy consultant working with blue-chip FMCG and Pharma clients;

- joined flutter.com (now Betfair) at early start-up stage in a senior business development role to help the team navigate through a very high growth period;

- part of a turn-around team at Littlewoods Gaming (Sportech plc) in a senior commercial development role;

- worked on the disposal of Redbus’ film distribution business before taking on a director role in its media assets division;

- senior member of the Redbus Media management team that has grown the business organically and by acquisition into one of the largest ‘destination’ media owners in the UK;

- senior member of the iwoca management team using technology to disrupt SME lending across Europe.

Farleys Solicitors LLP is a full service law firm providing a full range of legal services for individuals and businesses; with offices across the North West, in Blackburn, Burnley, Accrington, Rawtenstall, Preston & Manchester.

I specialise in employment law and HR for both employers and employees and sports law.

I am regularly instructed by:

•	Employers of all sizes and business sectors, including directors, senior managers, HR advisors and other decision-makers;
•	Employees from both the private and public sectors and from junior to senior executive and director level; 
•	Sports clubs and organisations, sports professionals and the Professional Footballer’s Association (PFA) and its members; 
•	Police officers and the Police Federation of England and Wales (PFEW); and
•	Regulated Professionals

I provide pragmatic, commercially focused advice and solutions on all areas of HR and employment law including:

•	Settlement agreements/termination/severance packages and negotiations,
•	Employee exits;
•	Employment disputes, Employment Tribunal claims & defence representation; 
•	Re-structures & redundancies;
•	Disciplinary, dismissal and grievance matters;
•	TUPE;
•	Performance management;
•	Sickness absence; 
•	Contracts of employment, staff handbooks, consultancy agreements and service agreements;
•	Unfair dismissal & constructive dismissal;
•	Breach of contract; 
•	Bullying and harassment, discrimination and whistleblowing; and
•	Early ACAS Conciliation. 

I am frequently consulted as an expert in employment law, HR and sports employment law by the media and also various publications including Lancashire Business View, Insider magazine, Radio Lancashire, Radio 5 Live, ITV’s Coronation Street and the BBC.
